HONESTY CLAUSES (non-severable disclosures, retained per project policy;
aligned with migration notes v2.1):

1. The attacker budget vector is printed alongside every readout; a
   readout without its budget is not interpretable. A single-shard
   readout decrease is not privacy (attacker-capacity dilution) —
   report the collusive ceiling max_C R(C) with the budget.
2. The 9-bit attacker ceiling is open (0.36 -> 0.42 -> 0.47 and rising
   with decoder capacity); every AMBER report carries a freshness label.
3. Entity-level recovery is measured at mechanism level on synthetic
   clinical notes only; real hospital PHI distributions remain untested.
4. Corpus x scale x family is confirmed at measured points (AG News /
   DBpedia / synthetic medical x 124M / 355M / Llama-1B); the ambient
   anchor varies with model scale, corpus, and family (Llama-1B:
   0.415) — per-deployment calibration is mandatory.
5. Label (R2) leakage is not reduced by bitrate: a 9-bit seam that
   reduces token recovery leaves label gist exposed. Class-is-sensitive
   deployments stay at RED.
6. This tool measures risk; it does not eliminate it. The remedy for a
   RED verdict is TEE, local inference, or not egressing at all.
7. AMBER boundary: 9-bit egress is applicable only when (a) the label
   is non-sensitive, (b) task output carries no sensitive content,
   (c) codebook statistics do not fingerprint the customer population,
   and (d) data volume makes local inference impractical. Ranking,
   credit-scoring, and diagnosis-class workloads are RED.
8. Detection granularity: certification is deployment-level, not
   query-level. One audit (about 2 GPU-hours) covers all queries under
   the same head and quantization configuration; quarterly re-audit
   (~30 min) plus event-triggered re-audit.
9. Codebook side channel: a 9-bit VQ codebook leaving the trust domain
   adds no token-recovery risk (measured), but its vector distribution
   may leak statistical properties of the training data — evaluate
   codebook statistical leakage, or fit the codebook on generic corpora.
10. Scope and variance: closed-source LLM scenarios are out of scope
   (there is no intermediate representation to measure). Probe
   training carries ~7pp run-to-run variance (exp18b); multi-seed
   averaging is mandatory before verdicts, and single-seed readouts
   with a large t5-t1 gap are refused (INCONCLUSIVE).
